    category: "Protocols",
    content: "# SG Mission Builder — Testing Mode Mission Design\n\n## What This Is\n\nTesting Mode is a slide-in panel in the Shir Glassworks admin app that guides Ori and Madeline through structured missions. Each mission walks them through a real workflow to test the app's features and capture feedback.\n\n## Your Role (Chat)\n\nYou design the **mission narrative** — the story, goals, and steps. You do NOT handle triggers, assistantContext, or deployment. That's Code's job.\n\n### What you produce:\n- Mission name, category, scenario, reflection prompts\n- Task list with clear goal descriptions\n- Which tasks are optional\n- Which tasks are prerequisites for other missions\n\n### What Code handles:\n- Mapping tasks to trigger events (auto-detection)\n- Writing assistantContext (requires reading the actual codebase)\n- Validating triggers exist in instrumented code\n- Adding new `emitTestingEvent()` calls if needed\n- Deploying to Firebase\n\n## Mission Design Schema\n\nWhen designing a mission, produce this structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"missionN\",\n  \"title\": \"Short descriptive title\",\n  \"category\": \"Selling|Making|Shipping|Marketing|Managing|Running\",\n  \"scenario\": \"1-2 sentence narrative — sets the scene\",\n  \"prePrompt\": \"Reflection question BEFORE tasks — captures baseline thinking\",\n  \"postPrompt\": \"Feedback question AFTER completion — captures experience and friction\",\n  \"sequence\": N,\n  \"requires\": null or \"missionN\",\n  \"preconditionNotice\": \"Optional — edge case warning for soft prerequisites\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"What the tester sees — a goal, not an instruction\",\n      \"optional\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Note:** Do NOT include `trigger` or `assistantContext` fields. Code adds these after reviewing the codebase.\n\n## Categories\n\n| Category | Emoji | Use For |\n|----------|-------|---------|\n| `Selling` | 🛒 | Orders, checkout, commissions, POS, events, customer-facing flows |\n| `Making` | 🔨 | Production jobs, builds, forecasting, line items |\n| `Shipping` | 📦 | Packing, labels, carrier handoff, fulfillment |\n| `Marketing` | 📣 | Social media, newsletters, content publishing |\n| `Managing` | 🗂️ | Products, inventory, settings, catalog management |\n| `Running` | 🏃 | Day-to-day business operations: trips, expenses, admin tasks |\n\n## Design Principles\n\n1. **Tasks are goals, not instructions.** \"Find the new order\" not \"Click Sell → Orders in the sidebar.\" The app's Studio Assistant handles directional hints.\n\n2. **Pre-prompts capture baseline.** Ask how they do this today, before the app shows them anything. This reveals gaps and assumptions.\n\n3. **Post-prompts capture friction.** Ask what felt clunky, what was missing, what surprised them. This is the primary feedback mechanism.\n\n4. **Scenarios set context.** Write them like a situation they'd actually face: \"A customer just placed an order\" or \"You've got a show coming up.\"\n\n5. **Optional tasks are conditional.** Use for things that only apply sometimes: \"Log losses if any pieces didn't turn out.\" These don't block mission completion.\n\n6. **Prerequisites are soft.** `requires` is informational — it tells the tester which mission should come first, but doesn't lock them out. Use `preconditionNotice` to explain what they need going in.\n\n7. **Keep missions focused.** 3-5 tasks per mission. If it needs more, split into two missions with a prerequisite chain.\n\n## Workflows File — IMPORTANT\n\nThe app's workflow documentation is a **YAML file**, not a markdown file. When a job spec says \"update workflows.md\", Code should locate the YAML equivalent (e.g. `workflows.yaml` or similar at repo root or `/docs/`). If neither exists, create `workflows.yaml` at repo root. Do NOT create a `.md` file for workflow documentation in this repo.\n\n## Handoff to Code\n\nWhen the mission design is ready, package it as a **job for Code** with:\n\n1. The mission JSON (without triggers/assistantContext)\n2. Brief notes on what each task does functionally (so Code knows which app functions to map)\n3. Any new app actions that might need instrumenting\n\n### Job format:\n\n```\nTitle: Deploy Mission N — {Mission Title}\n\nInstructions:\n1. Review the mission design below against the codebase\n2. Add trigger events to each task (or leave null for manual checkbox)\n3. Write assistantContext for each task based on actual UI\n4. Add any new emitTestingEvent() calls if needed\n5. Deploy to Firebase RTDB\n6. Commit and push\n\nMission Design:\n{paste the JSON}\n\nTask Notes:\n- Task 1: This involves [specific app action] — check if there's a trigger for it\n- Task 2: This is a manual verification step, probably no trigger\n- ...\n```\n\nUse the `job(start)` MCP tool with `createdBy: \"claude-chat\"` and `appId: \"shirglassworks\"` to create the job. Attach the mission design as an attachment with `type: \"spec\"`.\n\n## Existing Missions (for reference)\n\n| ID | Category | Title | Requires |\n|----|----------|-------|----------|\n| mission1 | Selling | From Website Order to UPS Drop-off | — |\n| mission2 | Making | Build What the Order Needs | mission1 |\n| mission3 | Selling | Plan a Craft Fair | — |\n| mission4 | Selling | Run the Fair | mission3 |\n| mission5 | Selling | Wrap Up After the Fair | mission4 |\n| mission6 | Making | Try Out a New Design | — |\n| mission7 | Making | Build for an Upcoming Event | — |\n| mission8 | Making | Build from Forecast | — |\n| mission9 | Marketing | Post a Video | — |\n| mission10 | Marketing | Write a Newsletter | — |\n| mission11 | Running | Log a Business Trip | — |\n\n## What's Already Covered\n\nBefore designing new missions, check what workflows are already tested:\n- **Order fulfillment:** mission1 (full order → ship flow)\n- **Production from orders:** mission2 (build request → complete → order advances)\n- **Craft fair lifecycle:** missions 3-5 (plan → run POS → wrap up)\n- **Product onboarding:** mission6 (create → photo → price → publish)\n- **Production planning:** missions 7-8 (manual job, forecast-driven job)\n- **Social media:** mission9 (clip → caption → post)\n- **Newsletter:** mission10 (create → write → publish)\n- **Business trips:** mission11 (start trip → destination → end → review history)\n\n**Gaps to consider:** Shipping (no dedicated mission yet), Commissions, Wholesale, Galleries, Customer management, Inventory transfers, Analytics review.",
